attorney general merrick garland is  calling on attorneys around the country  to volunteer and help people at risk of  being evicted  the legal profession is well positioned  to provide support for tenants landlords  and courts during this crisis  ensuring that our justice system  delivers outcomes that are fair and  accessible to all  without regard to wealth or status  is one of the highest ideals of our  profession  garland suggested that attorneys  volunteer with their local legal aid  provider or volunteer to mediate for the  courts on thursday the supreme court  struck down the eviction moratorium  extended by the cdc saying it must be  passed by congress  well the i-team has been covering  housing issues throughout southern  nevada and according to metro there was  a very slight dip in the number of  eviction notices delivered by the  constables office over the past couple  of weeks i hear the numbers from august  15 to the 21st the department reports  169 the following week 162 reported  vanessa murphy shared the story of one  woman who was evicted and eight news now  viewers responded with generosity  this gate was locked when karine cantino  was evicted she says she slept in her  car with her pets but thanks to some  generous eight news now viewers she is  now back in her home with her pets no  longer homeless karine  tell me what this experience has been  like for you  i am so grateful  for this lady that wants to remain  anonymous  she helped me tremendously and the power  of prayer is amazing  is amazing i am so blessed that she came  and helped me like she did she told us  she's a former metro employee but she  doesn't want to be named she came  forward and donated more than eight  thousand dollars and then there's also  this this gofundme which was over five  thousand dollars from other viewers i i  can't thank the people enough for for  helping me as much as they have  i really i owe you a big thank you  from all my heart i i just thank you i  appreciate you you're all earth angels a  new beginning for you and your pets  thanks for sharing your story thank you  vanessa thank you so much  you're welcome thank you we'll send it  back to you  karine contino by the way says one of  the issues she faced was just navigating  the whole rental assistance program also  known as chap and then getting answers  while she waited for her application to  be processed the i-team reached out to  the county and a spokesman says 8 500  applications are still waiting to be  processed we have information to help  both tenants and landlords at eight  newsnow dot com
 

